WEBVTT

00:05.171 --> 00:08.231
Machiavelli! You've told me nothing
I don't already know!

00:08.975 --> 00:11.239
Sun Tzu's The Art of War.

00:11.344 --> 00:15.110
Stewie, those books aren't
for babies. Here. Watch the Teletubbies.

00:15.382 --> 00:19.182
How dare you! That book may hold the key
to my enslaving of all mankind.

00:19.786 --> 00:20.582
Fuzzy.

00:21.888 --> 00:23.355
Tickle.

00:23.456 --> 00:27.449
God. The more I resist, the more intriguing
they become! I can't look away!

00:27.827 --> 00:29.260
Again! Again!

00:29.362 --> 00:32.798
Yes! Yes! Again! Again!
Dear God, please once more!

00:33.166 --> 00:34.155
Sorry, Stewie.

00:34.267 --> 00:37.236
A&E Biography is doing the life
of the other guy from Wham.

00:37.437 --> 00:41.305
I'm free! Free from the spell
of those diabolical Teletubbies!

00:41.408 --> 00:45.174
Thank you. When the world is mine,
your death shall be quick and painless.

00:45.945 --> 00:48.880
"It seems today that all you see

00:49.382 --> 00:52.476
"is violence in movies and sex on TV

00:52.852 --> 00:55.878
"But where are those good,
old-fashioned values

00:56.456 --> 00:58.617
"on which we used to rely?

00:59.459 --> 01:02.451
"Lucky there's a family guy

01:02.562 --> 01:05.656
"Lucky there's a man who'll
positively tell you

01:05.765 --> 01:07.494
"all the things that make us

01:07.600 --> 01:09.158
"laugh 'n' cry

01:09.335 --> 01:14.295
"He's a family guy"

01:17.844 --> 01:18.936
Attention, please.

01:19.045 --> 01:22.845
Tomorrow is softball practice. We have
a lot of work to do for Saturday's game.

01:22.949 --> 01:27.443
Don't forget how badly we were humiliated
last year by Pawtucket Joke and Novelties.

01:32.992 --> 01:35.927
Look at those morons
and their stupid glasses.

01:36.029 --> 01:37.496
Oh, man. I hate those guys.

01:37.597 --> 01:41.192
More than I hate spinach, traffic jams,
and the last few years of M* A*S*H.

01:41.301 --> 01:43.428
When Alan Alda took over
behind the camera...

01:43.536 --> 01:45.527
...and the show
got all dramatic and preachy?

01:45.638 --> 01:47.162
Am I right? Who's with me?

01:47.273 --> 01:50.606
This year we will defeat those Pranksters
with our secret weapon...

01:51.311 --> 01:52.710
...Guillermo.

01:55.381 --> 01:56.712
Bravo!

01:56.816 --> 02:00.377
I hired Guillermo because I believe
he'll be an asset to our company...

02:00.487 --> 02:01.920
...on and off the field.

02:02.355 --> 02:04.619
You have impeccable credentials.

02:04.824 --> 02:07.952
I'm sure I can find a position
for you somewhere.

02:08.328 --> 02:09.522
Back to work, people.

02:09.629 --> 02:13.190
Mr. Weed, I got a great idea for
a new line of TV action figures.

02:13.500 --> 02:16.992
Facts of Life Transformers, huh?
Watch the transformation.

02:17.437 --> 02:18.699
Cute as a button...

02:18.805 --> 02:20.238
...fat as a cow...

02:20.340 --> 02:25.107
...radioactive scorpion.
Watch out, Mrs. Garrett. Here comes Blair.

02:25.211 --> 02:27.145
- I'll consider it.
- He'll consider it!

02:27.247 --> 02:31.274
I got another one where Natalie's one of
those spittin' lizards from Jurassic Park.

02:36.222 --> 02:39.680
Pat, I would like to solve the puzzle.
"Go tuck yourself in. "

02:40.426 --> 02:41.450
You got it.

02:41.694 --> 02:43.252
Well, you were close, Dad.

02:43.363 --> 02:46.764
Yeah. I still can't believe we missed
the phrase, "My hairy aunt. "

02:46.900 --> 02:49.300
Come on, Brian.
I gotta get to softball practice.

02:49.402 --> 02:52.803
Practice? I thought we'd go next door
and welcome our new neighbors.

02:52.906 --> 02:55.238
No. I don't want anything to do
with neighbors.

02:55.341 --> 02:58.401
Last guy who lived next door
borrowed my toaster. Never saw it again.

02:59.279 --> 03:02.271
If that slut wants full custody of the kids,
she's got it.

03:04.851 --> 03:07.081
Peter, they might be very nice people.

03:07.187 --> 03:09.849
"Very nice people. "
Yeah, that's what they always say.

03:09.956 --> 03:13.448
Then you open up the septic tank and...
Skeleton city!

03:19.532 --> 03:20.726
Pervert!

03:21.034 --> 03:23.764
Don't flatter yourself, honey.
I don't have any sweat glands.

03:23.870 --> 03:27.237
Okay, time for batting practice,
my Happy-Go-Lucky Toy Boys.

03:27.340 --> 03:28.932
Guillermo, you're up.

03:29.342 --> 03:32.834
Unfortunately Johnson isn't here
to pitch today. His wife is in labor.

03:32.946 --> 03:35.813
Oh, what? Is the baby coming out of him?
Jeez, I'll pitch.

03:35.915 --> 03:39.976
I don't know what's more questionable,
your pitching arm or Bill Clinton's integrity.

03:40.086 --> 03:41.246
Oh, how hard...

03:45.592 --> 03:47.890
Oh, how hard can it be to pitch?

03:52.966 --> 03:56.163
- Okay. Take your base.
- Somebody call 911.

03:56.369 --> 03:59.361
Tell them he is allergic to penicillin
and white zinfandel!

03:59.472 --> 04:03.636
Idiot! If you don't find a ringer
to replace Guillermo, you're fired!

04:04.344 --> 04:07.643
Man. What'll I do if I get fired?
I'll have to go back to my old job...

04:07.747 --> 04:09.237
...as a Calvin Klein model.

04:09.382 --> 04:11.646
I don't wanna be like everyone else.

04:11.751 --> 04:13.343
But I don't want to be different.

04:13.453 --> 04:15.353
I just want to be.

04:16.889 --> 04:19.380
What was the name
of the bad guy from Tron?

04:20.593 --> 04:22.185
This is gonna drive me nuts!

04:22.829 --> 04:24.922
Moving is never easy on a family.

04:25.031 --> 04:28.523
Well, we are gonna miss
the go-go-go pace of Providence.

04:28.735 --> 04:32.034
But with number two on the way,
Joe thought it was time to move.

04:32.138 --> 04:35.801
And I can't say no to Joe. Ever.

04:36.576 --> 04:39.010
Quahog can be pretty exciting, too.

04:39.112 --> 04:41.478
Last week, someone lost an eye at Bingo.

04:41.781 --> 04:43.942
I-17. Darn it.

04:46.819 --> 04:49.117
I haven't played Bingo in years!

04:49.222 --> 04:53.318
Silence! Ever since you two met,
you've done nothing but wax idiotic!

04:53.426 --> 04:55.553
I must escape this infernal babble!

04:56.796 --> 04:58.764
What a little explorer.

04:58.865 --> 05:00.890
Yes. He's so full of wonder.

05:01.401 --> 05:03.801
To be the Lindbergh baby right about now.

05:04.937 --> 05:08.236
Joe, you have to meet
our new neighbor, Lois Griffin.

05:08.341 --> 05:10.639
It's a pleasure, Lois. Who's the little guy?

05:10.743 --> 05:14.201
This is Stewie.
Honey, say hi to Mr. Swanson.

05:14.514 --> 05:16.106
You will bow to me.

05:19.252 --> 05:21.948
Hi. I'm Meg. I live next door.

05:22.155 --> 05:25.124
I know.
I've admired you in the garden from afar.

05:25.291 --> 05:27.452
- Will you go out with me?
- I'd love to.

05:28.828 --> 05:30.955
Oh, he's gay.
You wish!

05:31.064 --> 05:33.191
Get out of here, you mouth breather!

05:33.399 --> 05:34.798
I'm as good as fired.

05:34.901 --> 05:37.734
Where the hell am I gonna find a guy
as strong as Guillermo?

05:37.837 --> 05:41.773
One time I walked into the locker room,
I swear he was bench-pressing Mr. Weed.

05:42.508 --> 05:45.272
Great. Lois is getting chummy
with the new neighbors.

05:45.378 --> 05:49.212
She wants you to meet them.
She's always making me be social.

05:49.315 --> 05:52.910
Cocktail parties, school functions,
that time we planted trees in Jerusalem.

05:53.720 --> 05:57.520
What? Look, all I'm saying is
put an Israeli guy next to an Arab guy...

05:57.623 --> 05:59.454
...and I can't tell the difference.

05:59.625 --> 06:02.992
- You must be Peter. Joe Swanson.
- Yeah, yeah. Nice to meet you, Phil.

06:03.096 --> 06:05.826
You got a neighbor
on the other side of your house, too.

06:05.932 --> 06:08.230
So, don't think you always have to bug me.

06:08.334 --> 06:11.565
I'll keep that in mind. Say, do you have
a screwdriver I can borrow?

06:11.671 --> 06:14.765
Man, you neighbors are like viruses.
Starts with a screwdriver.

06:14.874 --> 06:17.104
Before you know it,
you're using my supermarket...

06:17.210 --> 06:19.269
...my dry cleaner, and even my postman.

06:19.379 --> 06:22.974
Can you believe that guy?
"Do you have a screwdriver I can borrow?"

06:23.082 --> 06:24.049
What an ass.

06:25.685 --> 06:29.553
- Did you find a replacement for the team?
- No. Believe me, I've been looking.

06:29.655 --> 06:32.055
Hideo-san would be honored to play
for your team.

06:32.158 --> 06:34.592
But he wishes to know
what compensation you offer.

06:35.928 --> 06:37.759
Me love you long time.

06:37.864 --> 06:40.731
Gosh, I'd like to help.
But I've gotta go out in the hall...

06:40.833 --> 06:42.767
...and chew on my ass for five minutes.

06:42.902 --> 06:45.962
Peter, I invited Joe and Bonnie
to your game on Saturday.

06:46.406 --> 06:48.397
Lois, I don't want those people there.

06:48.508 --> 06:51.909
See, this is why I ask you
to submit everything to me in writing first.

06:52.011 --> 06:55.845
Bonnie told me Joe is a big baseball fan.
He played in college.

06:56.449 --> 06:57.313
He did?

06:57.717 --> 06:59.184
Welcome to the neighborhood.

06:59.285 --> 07:00.115
Hiya, Joe.

07:00.219 --> 07:01.481
- Peter!
- Don't get up.

07:01.587 --> 07:04.215
This is a surprise.
I kinda thought you didn't like me.

07:04.323 --> 07:06.757
What? Because of what I said
this afternoon. No.

07:06.859 --> 07:09.794
See I have that disease
where stuff pops out of your mouth.

07:09.896 --> 07:12.194
Go to hell! Whoops. See what I mean?

07:13.032 --> 07:14.192
I'm so sorry.

07:14.567 --> 07:18.094
I thought maybe I crossed the line
when I asked to borrow a screwdriver.

07:18.971 --> 07:21.565
Are you kidding?
You can borrow whatever you want.

07:21.674 --> 07:24.905
Great. Say, you don't happen
to have any picture wire, do you?

07:25.011 --> 07:27.172
Picture wire? You son of a bitch.

07:28.881 --> 07:31.406
Son of a bitch! Son of a bitch!
There it goes again.

07:31.517 --> 07:32.848
I don't want to impose.

07:32.952 --> 07:35.921
No problem. That's what neighbors do.
You know what else they do?

07:36.022 --> 07:39.355
They play on their neighbor's company
softball team like this Saturday.

07:39.459 --> 07:41.620
What do you say, neighbor?
Sounds fun.

07:41.727 --> 07:45.458
So much fun it should be illegal
like copyright infringement.

07:46.265 --> 07:48.062
See you at the game, Joe.

07:52.905 --> 07:55.339
- Hey, you want a piece of gum?
- Thanks.

07:55.975 --> 07:58.000
- That was joke gum.
- What do you mean?

07:58.110 --> 07:59.737
Now you're addicted to heroin.

08:02.915 --> 08:03.904
I'm cold.

08:04.150 --> 08:05.208
Hey, Peter!

08:05.551 --> 08:07.781
It's nice that your family is here.

08:07.887 --> 08:11.448
If your ringer doesn't arrive soon,
you can spend every day with them...

08:11.557 --> 08:12.649
...at home.

08:12.758 --> 08:15.556
He'll be here, Mr. Weed.
You should see this guy in action.

08:15.661 --> 08:17.652
He can hit, he can throw...
Peter!

08:17.763 --> 08:20.061
What's he doing in a wheelchair?

08:20.533 --> 08:22.694
Holy crip, he's a crapple!

08:25.471 --> 08:30.374
Peter, our new secret weapon
is this very attractive paraplegic?

08:30.977 --> 08:34.071
Okay, Joe, you got me.
Rise and shine. Come on.

08:34.180 --> 08:38.276
- Stand and deliver. Get the hell up.
- You're a hoot, Peter.

08:38.384 --> 08:40.284
- Play ball!
- Let's do it!

08:40.386 --> 08:43.583
I swear I didn't know.
Maybe they won't hit a lot of balls to him.

08:43.689 --> 08:45.247
I got shortstop.

08:45.958 --> 08:48.290
The movers tracked grease
all over my carpet.

08:48.394 --> 08:51.488
- I tried everything to get the stain out.
- What about lemon juice?

08:51.597 --> 08:54.327
- What about club soda?
- What about shutting the hell up?

08:54.800 --> 08:56.563
Isn't baseball great?

08:57.737 --> 09:00.467
They say baseball's the national pastime.

09:02.408 --> 09:03.739
I can't taste salt.

09:06.112 --> 09:09.741
Crap! Don't hit it to Joe.
Please don't hit it to Joe!

09:15.354 --> 09:16.582
You're out!

09:17.590 --> 09:20.286
All right, Joe!
Way to earn that parking space!

09:20.393 --> 09:22.224
All right!
Did you see that?

09:22.328 --> 09:24.387
That's my Joe!
What the deuce?

09:24.830 --> 09:26.730
Half man, half machine.

09:27.099 --> 09:30.500
Why with that technology,
I could escape these wretched harridans!

09:30.603 --> 09:31.934
Go, cyborg!

09:36.409 --> 09:39.742
It all rests on that man's broad,
rippling shoulders!

09:41.981 --> 09:43.608
All right, Joe! Run!

09:43.716 --> 09:45.911
All right, Joe! Come on! Yeah!

09:49.021 --> 09:52.115
Hurry! Joe!
All right! Yes, vamos!

09:56.295 --> 09:57.956
Let's hear it for Joe!

09:58.064 --> 10:00.532
Yeah, let's hear it for the guy
who found Joe!

10:01.601 --> 10:02.397
Okay.

10:06.205 --> 10:10.141
That's finger suckin' good, huh?
It's an old policemen's recipe.

10:10.276 --> 10:14.804
Eat up, everyone. Tonight my wife won't
be the only one enjoying a pig in a blanket.

10:15.715 --> 10:17.478
Joe, you're so funny.

10:18.250 --> 10:20.411
They love that one down at the Precinct.

10:21.187 --> 10:23.553
This sucks, Brian.
Joe is stealing my thunder.

10:23.656 --> 10:26.523
Hey, everybody! Time to limbo!

10:26.626 --> 10:28.924
- Face it. He's the life of the party.
- Yeah?

10:29.028 --> 10:31.326
I'll show you who's the life of the party.

10:31.564 --> 10:34.499
Hey, look!
I fell in the pool with my clothes on!

10:34.700 --> 10:38.830
How hilarious is that?
That is so Peter Griffin. Guys?

10:39.772 --> 10:40.761
Guys?

10:42.341 --> 10:44.707
That's my idea.
Peter, come here.

10:44.810 --> 10:46.505
Finally. A little recognition.

10:46.612 --> 10:48.580
Joe has the most wonderful idea.

10:48.681 --> 10:52.344
Hey, I just suggested a line
of handi-capable toys, you know...

10:52.451 --> 10:55.511
...to show kids the fun side
of being physically challenged!

10:55.788 --> 10:59.280
That's what kids want to play with.
Yeah. A Beanie Baby in a bubble.

10:59.392 --> 11:02.520
What about my idea? Come on!
Tootie morphs into a stink bug.

11:02.628 --> 11:05.961
Joe, you're exactly the kind of man
we need at our company.

11:06.165 --> 11:08.668
Peter, make yourself useful.
Go get Joe a drink.

11:08.868 --> 11:11.530
Jeez, first he takes my friends.
Then he takes my job.

11:11.637 --> 11:13.332
But the way I wear my hat...

11:13.773 --> 11:16.207
No, no. He can't take that away from me.

11:16.676 --> 11:19.440
You! How came you
by this metal construct?

11:19.812 --> 11:23.543
- I demand to know who made you!
- Stewie, it's not polite to point.

11:23.649 --> 11:25.048
I'm so sorry.

11:25.151 --> 11:28.587
That's okay, Lois.
He's just curious about the chair.

11:28.688 --> 11:32.146
About 10 years ago I was investigating
a robbery at an orphanage.

11:32.525 --> 11:35.460
It was Christmas Eve
and some presents had been stolen.

11:45.171 --> 11:46.934
Reach for the sky, dirtbag!

11:47.907 --> 11:50.740
All right, pal!
You've stolen your last Christmas.

12:19.672 --> 12:22.869
"You think you have won
You think all is well

12:22.975 --> 12:26.672
"But kiss my green ass
I shall see you in hell!"

12:35.855 --> 12:37.049
Are you Timmy?

12:38.457 --> 12:40.049
Merry Christmas, Timmy.

12:42.528 --> 12:43.256
Enough!

12:43.362 --> 12:46.559
If you won't share your technological
schemata with me peaceably...

12:46.665 --> 12:49.498
...I shall take the information
from you by force!

12:49.635 --> 12:52.126
Wow. Looks like you have a fan.

12:52.238 --> 12:54.968
- Come on. Let's get out of here.
- Peter, you can't leave.

12:55.074 --> 12:56.871
Sorry, I promised the wife and kids I'd...

12:56.976 --> 13:01.379
...take them on a dream vacation
to Hawaii right now. Say aloha, kids.

13:01.480 --> 13:05.143
What are you talking about? We want to
hear more of Mr. Swanson's stories.

13:05.251 --> 13:07.481
He's cool, Dad. He killed a guy.

13:07.586 --> 13:11.647
Well, technically he was killed by the state,
but funny story.

13:11.891 --> 13:14.917
He did curse my name
just before the injection.

13:17.763 --> 13:19.628
Peter, what's the matter with you?

13:19.732 --> 13:21.859
Why are you guys making such a big deal
over Joe?

13:21.967 --> 13:25.596
You don't admire wheelchair people.
You're supposed to feel sorry for them.

13:25.704 --> 13:27.695
When did it become okay
to be handicapped?

13:27.807 --> 13:29.172
Don't talk like that!

13:29.275 --> 13:32.005
He's a remarkable man
and the rest of your family adores him!

13:32.111 --> 13:34.238
Fine. Then why don't you all marry him?

13:34.346 --> 13:37.281
And if he's so remarkable,
let's see him do this.

13:37.683 --> 13:41.642
Hey, look at me. I'm walking.
I'm a remarkable man.

13:46.292 --> 13:48.157
Well, look who finally came home.

13:48.260 --> 13:50.854
I thought you were gonna spend
all night at Joe's.

13:50.963 --> 13:53.830
I could've. That man has got magic fingers.

13:53.933 --> 13:56.367
He found this one spot behind my ear, I...

13:56.468 --> 13:58.959
Forget about it.
I thought my leg was never gonna stop.

13:59.071 --> 14:00.129
I don't believe this.

14:00.239 --> 14:03.003
My whole family worships the ground
that guy can't walk on.

14:03.108 --> 14:06.874
It's not too hard to see why. He's a hero.
He makes the world a better place.

14:07.012 --> 14:08.980
I've done lots of things to help people.

14:09.081 --> 14:11.743
Remember the time I sang to the kids
at the Sunday school?

14:11.851 --> 14:13.011
Yes, you forgot the words.

14:13.285 --> 14:14.547
"Jesus loves me

14:14.987 --> 14:16.716
"He loves me a bunch

14:16.822 --> 14:18.790
"Because He always puts Skippy

14:18.958 --> 14:20.482
"In my lunch"

14:21.527 --> 14:25.258
No. It's not the same thing.
Joe puts himself in real danger every day.

14:25.364 --> 14:27.992
You're right. I'll never be that kind of hero.

14:28.567 --> 14:32.298
Unless I put myself in real danger, too!
For my family's sake!

14:33.339 --> 14:35.739
Why are the pretty ones
always so dumb?

14:47.953 --> 14:51.116
Gang shooting on
Third and Main. Three wounded, one dead.

14:51.223 --> 14:55.057
- Is it me or is rap music just getting lazier?
- No. It's my new police scanner.

14:55.160 --> 14:58.095
This hero thing is gonna be easy
once I find the right crime.

14:58.197 --> 15:00.324
Domestic disturbance...
Boring!

15:00.466 --> 15:01.865
Report of a stabbing in...

15:02.835 --> 15:06.430
All units! A major robbery
is in progress at Quahog Bank and Trust.

15:06.538 --> 15:08.699
Suspects are armed
and extremely dangerous.

15:08.807 --> 15:11.241
- Perfect! Where's Lois and the kids?
- Over at Joe's.

15:11.343 --> 15:12.275
Well, go fetch 'em.

15:12.378 --> 15:15.814
They're about to see a real hero in action.
To the Batcave!

15:24.924 --> 15:27.449
Oh, God! Oh, God! Oh, God!

15:30.095 --> 15:33.428
You thought Joe was something.
You ain't seen nothin' yet.

15:33.532 --> 15:35.523
Peter, what's the big rush?

15:36.268 --> 15:37.792
All right, you guys wait right here.

15:37.903 --> 15:39.666
Daddy's gonna make a little withdrawal.

15:41.340 --> 15:43.069
Give Tammy a round of applause.

15:43.175 --> 15:46.338
This was her first robbery
and she was very brave.

15:48.414 --> 15:49.608
Now before we go...

15:49.715 --> 15:51.148
No, don't go.

15:51.250 --> 15:52.683
Oh, princess, we have to.

15:52.785 --> 15:55.117
I hope you brought
your striped pajamas, boys.

15:55.220 --> 15:58.747
Because there's a five-year sleepover
at the big house. And you're invited.

15:58.891 --> 16:00.620
You'll never take us alive!

16:02.294 --> 16:04.489
Lois and the kids
should be in here to see this.

16:04.596 --> 16:06.188
Yes. It's going very well.

16:06.298 --> 16:09.631
Mom, what do you do when you like a boy
but he doesn't even notice you?

16:09.735 --> 16:11.362
Meg loves Kevin.

16:11.470 --> 16:13.097
Shut up, you big sack of dog vomit!

16:13.205 --> 16:16.470
Meg, you're a sweet, lovely girl.
He'll come around.

16:16.909 --> 16:18.240
Such a mom answer.

16:18.344 --> 16:22.610
Have you tried showing off the goods?
How's that for a mom answer?

16:22.948 --> 16:24.108
Creepy.

16:24.216 --> 16:26.411
I saw some cute dresses down the street.

16:26.518 --> 16:29.612
If nothing else, it'll make you feel better.
Come on, you guys.

16:29.755 --> 16:32.588
If you want to be a hero,
now might be a good time.

16:33.025 --> 16:34.390
This isn't what I was expecting.

16:34.493 --> 16:36.484
I thought being a hero
would be all fun and games.

16:39.565 --> 16:43.262
Sorry, Wonder Woman.
I got three kings. Now let's see your pair.

16:45.337 --> 16:48.966
All right. Robin, what are you looking
at me for? Look at her.

16:50.476 --> 16:51.875
Come on. Let's go.

16:51.977 --> 16:52.909
Oh, perfect.

16:53.245 --> 16:55.475
We got hostages!
Don't try anything funny!

16:56.048 --> 16:57.572
Don't worry, Brian. I got a plan.

16:57.716 --> 17:00.082
Good. I was afraid
you were just gonna improvise.

17:00.185 --> 17:03.018
Actually, I was gonna use
the little girl as a human shield...

17:03.122 --> 17:03.986
...and run like hell.

17:04.089 --> 17:06.387
But improvise, that'll be easier on my back.

17:08.127 --> 17:12.257
Okay, in this improv, Tammy and
the short robber are husband and wife.

17:13.065 --> 17:14.862
Okay. And where are we?
A bar!

17:14.967 --> 17:17.401
A pet store!
Guadalajara, Mexico!

17:17.503 --> 17:20.904
Okay, okay. I heard pet store.
And I'm the gruff but lovable owner.

17:21.006 --> 17:25.238
All right. Begin. Hello, married couple.
I see you found a puppy.

17:25.344 --> 17:26.971
Yeah. His name is Sparky.

17:27.079 --> 17:30.879
Well, before you take Sparky home,
let me check him for worms.

17:31.817 --> 17:33.307
Okay, drop it!

17:36.655 --> 17:39.453
All right, you guys. Let's get out of here.

17:42.027 --> 17:43.153
All right, stand back!

17:43.262 --> 17:46.026
Whoa. Hang on. Sorry, no one can leave.

17:46.865 --> 17:50.392
Listen, the whole reason I saved
you guys today was so I could be a hero.

17:50.702 --> 17:55.435
This wheelchair guy moved in next door
and he can do all these great things and...

17:55.674 --> 17:58.700
Your family idolizes the lousy cripple
and not you?

17:58.811 --> 18:00.244
That's right! How'd you know?

18:00.345 --> 18:01.812
We've all been there.

18:02.347 --> 18:04.713
Cool! The bank is getting jacked!

18:04.883 --> 18:06.475
Officer, my husband's in there!

18:06.585 --> 18:09.110
- Can you tell me if he's okay?
- What's he look like?

18:09.221 --> 18:13.624
He's wearing a white-collared shirt,
kind of big, with glasses.

18:13.759 --> 18:15.522
I got him.
Oh, thank God.

18:15.627 --> 18:17.288
- Take him out.
- No!

18:17.696 --> 18:18.924
Hey, there's my family.

18:19.031 --> 18:20.726
I just want you to know I rob banks...

18:20.833 --> 18:23.563
...because a deaf man stole my job
at the phone company.

18:23.669 --> 18:26.729
So if anyone's gonna bust me,
I'm glad it's you.

18:28.373 --> 18:30.603
But... But I was gonna be a hero.

18:30.709 --> 18:32.108
Nobody's going anywhere!

18:34.246 --> 18:36.544
Joe, it's Peter! He's in trouble!

18:36.748 --> 18:38.807
A failed robbery at
Quahog Bank and Trust...

18:38.917 --> 18:41.715
...has led to a terrifying hostage situation.

18:44.423 --> 18:46.288
That's right. A hostage situation.

18:46.391 --> 18:48.859
- I gotta go.
- I know.

18:49.661 --> 18:53.825
If we want the cops to take us seriously,
we have to waste a hostage. But who?

18:53.966 --> 18:56.696
- Excuse me. Shouldn't that be "whom"?
- Okay, you.

18:56.802 --> 18:57.700
Crap!

18:57.803 --> 19:01.295
This is Police Lieutenant
Joe Swanson. I know we can work this out.

19:01.740 --> 19:04.641
Not him again. I hope this place
isn't wheelchair accessible.

19:04.776 --> 19:06.107
Bonnie, it's Peter.

19:06.211 --> 19:08.702
Don't worry.
Joe's an excellent negotiator.

19:09.114 --> 19:12.379
I was a virgin when we met.
It took him three hours.

19:14.686 --> 19:17.018
I can't believe my dad is in there.

19:18.056 --> 19:20.581
This'll probably scar me
for the rest of my life.

19:21.927 --> 19:23.656
I got a new dress.

19:23.762 --> 19:25.593
Try talking about him.

19:26.331 --> 19:28.526
So do you like music?

19:28.667 --> 19:30.862
Yeah! I played guitar
in a band before we moved.

19:30.969 --> 19:33.597
But it interfered with my studies.
What do you listen to?

19:33.805 --> 19:34.772
You first.

19:34.973 --> 19:37.032
I'm into Garbage, Phish, Blur.

19:37.142 --> 19:39.303
My parents don't like me
listening to that stuff.

19:39.411 --> 19:42.141
But I do anyway because I am not a robot!

19:43.182 --> 19:44.809
I also like Radiohead.

19:44.917 --> 19:48.148
And even though society has turned
its back on you...

19:48.487 --> 19:50.955
...I promise you there are people who care.

19:51.056 --> 19:53.286
And you know what? I'm one of them.

19:53.525 --> 19:54.617
He sure gets it.

19:54.726 --> 19:56.717
Maybe he's right.
We can make a new start.

19:56.828 --> 19:58.056
Come on, guys.

19:58.163 --> 20:00.097
Don't let him sweet talk you like that.

20:00.332 --> 20:01.560
Wait. You can't leave now.

20:01.667 --> 20:03.635
I'm supposed to be the hero. Wait!

20:03.735 --> 20:06.670
Can you let me pistol-whip you
a couple times for the camera?

20:07.105 --> 20:11.565
Stupid robbers with your guns
and your make-out parties.

20:20.285 --> 20:21.047
Excellent!

20:21.153 --> 20:23.781
They detached the human component
from the machine.

20:23.889 --> 20:27.586
Machine, I am your new master
and I order you to go!

20:28.026 --> 20:28.993
Engage!

20:29.494 --> 20:32.827
Blast! Must be some kind of
proprietary command system.

20:33.031 --> 20:35.465
Now on the Russian MiG,
it's next to the altimeter.

20:35.567 --> 20:38.764
There you are.
I can't turn my back on you for a second.

20:39.538 --> 20:42.132
One day I shall unlock the secret
of that device.

20:42.241 --> 20:44.334
And when I do, Mother, victory shall be...

20:47.746 --> 20:52.206
Peter, you had us so worried.
What on earth were you trying to prove?

20:52.417 --> 20:54.783
I'm sorry. Joe is a great guy.

20:54.886 --> 20:57.286
I guess I was just tired of him
being your hero.

20:57.389 --> 21:00.756
Peter, Joe is a hero. But he's not our hero.

21:00.859 --> 21:02.258
- You are.
- Really?

21:02.494 --> 21:03.518
Yeah.

21:03.629 --> 21:08.293
You're always right there on the couch
for us, making us laugh when we're upset.

21:08.600 --> 21:11.535
Changing the channel
when something boring comes on.

21:11.637 --> 21:14.936
Eating the last slice of pizza
so the rest of us don't fight over it.

21:15.040 --> 21:17.031
Yeah, Daddy.
If you hadn't pulled this stunt...

21:17.142 --> 21:19.235
...I wouldn't know
how to manipulate Kevin.

21:19.344 --> 21:21.835
And when the kids at school see us on TV...

21:21.947 --> 21:26.907
...they'll think you're a total psycho.
And I can say, "That psycho is my dad!"

21:27.486 --> 21:30.182
I wouldn't have won silver in Nagano,
had you not driven me...

21:30.289 --> 21:32.314
...to the ice rink every morning at 6:00 a. m.

21:33.158 --> 21:37.322
I guess being a hero isn't always
about saving lives and catching bad guys.

21:37.429 --> 21:40.057
It's also about just being there
for the people you love.

21:40.165 --> 21:42.133
Help!
Someone just stole my purse!

21:42.234 --> 21:44.600
Who cares? I don't even know you.

21:44.601 --> 23:45.601
Thank you for watching «Family Guy» on
www.FOX-fan.ru